{
  "pedal": "Boss AW-3 Dynamic Wah, Up mode (mono: Guitar input -> Output)",
  "comment": "Up mode in full: Manual at all eleven hour positions (the filter at rest; at the end, as a first pass turned Sens instead — kept as rest-sens-*), Sens and Decay at five, Manual's effect on the swept range at both ends, picked notes at three Decays. Guitar input -> Output, nothing in EXP, adapter power. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; Manual's printed marks at 9:00, 11:00 and 1:00. Sweeps at -36 dB with Sens at minimum: the filter at rest (the envelope shouldn't move it). Noise staircases (-54 to +3 dB, 1.5 s a step): where the filter settles at each input level, read from the noise's spectrum against the bypass staircase (same seed). Noise jumps (-48 / 0 / -48 dB, 4 s each): how fast it opens and how it falls back (Decay). Takes ordered by setting, for the fewest knob turns.",
